.TH LIBTLS_TLS_ACCEPT 3 "2023-04-01" "libtls" "TLS Library"
.SH NAME
tls_accept - Accept a TLS connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libtls.h>
.sp
.B int
.B tls_accept(int fd);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B tls_accept
function accepts a TLS connection on a file descriptor.
The
.B fd
argument is the file descriptor to accept the TLS connection on.
The function waits for a TLS client to initiate a connection and completes the TLS handshake.
The function returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure with
.B errno
set to indicate the error.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B tls_accept
function to accept a TLS connection:
.nf
.B #include <libtls.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   int fd = 0; // Assume a valid file descriptor
.B   int ret = tls_accept(fd);
.B   if(ret == 0) {
.B     printf("TLS connection accepted\n");
.B   } else {
.B     perror("tls_accept");
.B   }
.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B libtls,
.B tls_connect(3),
.B tls_read(3),
.B tls_write(3)